5... h6 { Black might play this move immediately thinking "oh, white has to move back to h3, what a bad situation!" But now we strike them with... } 6. Nxf7! { The move that signals danger for black's position. Now black will have to play accurately to avoid destruction of their king. } 6... Kxf7 7. Ne5+! { From here, blacks king has only one move in this position, Kg8. First we should analyze bad moves for blacks king and punish their mistakes. } 7... Ke8 8. Bd3 { Aiming for the light squares, which are weak in blacks position. } 8... e6 9. Bg6+ Ke7 10. Nf7 { Setting up a fork of the rook and the queen. } 10... Qd5 11. O-O! { Make sure not to take the rook! Qxg2 would mess things up for your plans. } 11... Rg8 12. d4 Bd7 13. Bf4 Be8 14. c4 Qa5 15. Bd6+ Kd7 { And I dont think you need an engine to tell that black is in trouble. } *


