7... Kg8 { By far best move for black } 8. Bc4+ e6 9. d4 Bd6 { Black tries to challenge this knight off the board and quickly trade pieces } 10. f4 Bxe5? { This is a big mistake for black as it allows for white to get an open F file, which will come to haunt black. } 11. fxe5 Nd5 12. O-O! { Immediately activating the rook on the most open file available. } 12... Nd7? 13. Qh5 Nf8 14. Qf7+ { Black resigned here. This was a real game between Jeremy Kane (the inventor) and Anna M. Sargsyan and it goes to show how dangerous this opening can be! } *


