7... c5! { The best move for black. } 8. c3 (8. Bc4+ e6 9. Ne5+ Kg8 10. Be3 cxd4 11. Bxd4) 8... Nc6 (8... e6 { [%csl Gf1] } 9. Bd3 Nc6 (9... cxd4 10. cxd4 Bb4+ 11. Kf1 Re8 12. Ne5+ Kg8 13. Bxh6 (13. h4))) 9. Bd3 cxd4 (9... e6) 10. O-O! { Dont waste time recapturing the d pawn, get right to work! } 10... dxc3 11. Re1 e6 (11... cxb2? 12. Bxb2 e6 13. Ne5+ { This move seems like a trade but it sets up something really special... } 13... Nxe5 14. Bg6+!! { The queens are staring at each other, but the king is more important! } 14... Nxg6 15. Qxd8 { And both sides are quite equal here. }) 12. bxc3 Bd6 13. Rb1 { And Black has a good position, but white can create quick attacks that can damage positions. } *


